## ⭐ CANONICAL REFERENCE — Dropdown / menu / flyout with animated expand-collapse

**Define ONE canonical dropdown/menu/flyout component for the project and reuse it in every NEW or refactored dropdown — never reimplement per screen.** Once the canonical component exists, record its path in THIS block (this file is the project's operational source of truth).

- **Animation anti-pattern:** NEVER `scaleY` on an overlay that contains text (it distorts the text during the animation). The recommended pattern is **clip-path inset + translateY + opacity**, with the opening longer than the close and per-side variants (`[data-side=top]` etc.).
- **Reduced-motion:** every overlay animation must be covered by a global `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` block.
- **Mandatory neutral color:** overlay content uses the design system's neutral popover token, **never a hardcoded brand color**.
- For INLINE accordion/expand-collapse (non-overlay) the animatable pattern is `grid grid-rows-[0fr→1fr]` + a child with `overflow-hidden` (`display:block/hidden` does NOT animate).

## ⭐ CANONICAL REFERENCE — Charts & Dashboards = 1 canonical library

**Adopt ONE canonical chart library for the project and record it in THIS block. Every NEW or refactored chart / dashboard / KPI-card uses the canonical library by default — do not introduce parallel libraries out of convenience.**

- **FALLBACK CLAUSE (honest — "canonical except where it doesn't exist"):** if the canonical library does NOT have the component for a chart type (e.g. **funnel**/drop-off, **heatmap**/matrix), the order is: (1) compose it with the primitives of the SAME base as the canonical library (keeps visual coherence); (2) only then the chart lib the app already uses. **Every exception is documented** (which chart, why). Introducing an additional chart library without justification is forbidden.
- **Prototype ≠ production:** a throwaway prototype (e.g. static HTML to validate the data story with stakeholders) NEVER becomes production code — the final dashboard is reimplemented in the canonical library.

